1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,233
Costco has sold a hot dog and a soda for $1.50 since 1985. On purpose.

2
00:00:06,403 --> 00:00:12,324
When the CEO said they were losing money, the founder replied: "If you raise the hot dog, I will kill you."

3
00:00:12,544 --> 00:00:15,360
Because the hot dog isn't the product. You are.

4
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:20,119
A cheap hot dog makes the whole store feel cheap, so you keep renewing your membership.

5
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:22,842
And memberships bring in most of Costco's profit.

6
00:00:23,012 --> 00:00:24,366
It's called a loss leader.

7
00:00:24,536 --> 00:00:28,019
So next time something feels too cheap, ask what it's really selling.
